    "steps": [
      "Stir the feta, parsley, chile flakes, olive oil and crushed coriander seeds together in a small bowl. Leave it to sit while you cook.",
      "Warm the remaining olive oil in a large lidded sauté pan set on medium-high. Cook the onion for 5 minutes, until soft and lightly browned.",
      "Add the red bell pepper strips and keep cooking for 5 minutes more.",
      "Stir in the garlic, paprika, tomato paste, cumin seeds and coriander seeds. Cook for 1 minute, until fragrant.",
      "Add the chopped tomatoes, cherry tomatoes, shatta and water. Season with salt and plenty of black pepper.",
      "Simmer on medium heat for roughly 15 minutes, until the sauce is thick and the tomatoes have collapsed.",
      "Season the beaten eggs with a little salt and black pepper in a bowl.",
      "Pour the eggs in slowly while swirling the pan, then fold gently. Turn the burner down to medium-low, put the lid on and cook 4 minutes, until softly set.",
      "Take the pan off the heat and spoon the feta mixture over the top. Sprinkle with the last chile flakes and serve at once.",
      "You nailed it! Grab a plate and dig in."
